ed actions","Allowing group-based access works only with a subject type of user by syncing users and their groups. If your configured key resolves to workload for a session, group-based access isn't supported.":"Allowing group-based access works only with a subject type of user by syncing users and their groups. If your configured key resolves to workload for a session, group-based access isn't supported.","Allowing password recovery for AWS Account {{accountId}}.":"Allowing password recovery for AWS Account {{accountId}}.","Allows users federated by the specified external web identity provider to assume this role to perform actions in this account.":"Allows users federated by the specified external web identity provider to assume this role to perform actions in this account.","Also known as client ID, audience is a value that identifies the application that is registered with an OpenID Connect provider.":"Also known as client ID, audience is a value that identifies the application that is registered with an OpenID Connect provider.","Alternative recommended":"Alternative recommended","Alternatives recommended":"Alternatives recommended","Alternatives to root user access keys":"Alternatives to root user access keys","Always active":"Always active","Always include default template":"Always include default template","Amazon Bedrock API keys":"Amazon Bedrock API keys","Amazon Keyspaces credentials":"Amazon Keyspaces credentials","Amazon Resource Name (ARN)":"Amazon Resource Name (ARN)","Amazon Web Services China (Beijing) Region endpoint":"Amazon Web Services China (Beijing) Region endpoint","Amazon Web Services China (Ningxia) Region endpoint":"Amazon Web Services China (Ningxia) Region endpoint","An AWS account":"An AWS account","An error occured while loading the policy editor.":"An error occured while loading the policy editor.","An error occurred":"An error occurred","An error occurred while loading the authorization details.":"An error occurred while loading the authorization details.","An IAM role is an identity you can create that has specific permissions with credentials that are valid for short durations. Roles can be assumed by entities that you trust.":"An IAM role is an identity you can create that has specific permissions with credentials that are valid for short durations. Roles can be assumed by entities that you trust.","An IAM user is an entity that you create in AWS to represent the person or application that uses it to interact with AWS.":"An IAM user is an entity that you create in AWS to represent the person or application that uses it to interact with AWS.","An IAM user is an identity with long-term credentials that is used to interact with AWS in an account.":"An IAM user is an identity with long-term credentials that is used to interact with AWS in an account.","An IAM user is created in this account. As a best practice, create IAM users only if you need to enable programmatic access through access keys, service-specific credentials for AWS CodeCommit or Amazon Keyspaces, or a backup credential for emergency account access.":"An IAM user is created in this account. As a best practice, create IAM users only if you need to enable programmatic access through access keys, service-specific credentials for AWS CodeCommit or Amazon Keyspaces, or a backup credential for emergency account access.","An internal error occurred. It's our fault, not yours. Wait a few minutes and try again. If the problem persists, contact AWS Customer Support.":"An internal error occurred. It's our fault, not yours. Wait a few minutes and try again. If the problem persists, contact AWS Customer Support.","Analyzer settings":"Analyzer settings",Analyzers:ti,and:"and","and {{num}} more.":"and {{num}} more.","and not":"and not","Another AWS account":"Another AWS account",Any:"Any","API key":"API key","API key expiration":"API key expiration","API key generated successfully.":"API key generated successfully.","API key name":"API key name","API key selection":"API key selection","API keys":"API keys","API keys for Amazon Bedrock":"API keys for Amazon Bedrock","API keys grant access to specific AWS services. You can have a maximum of two API keys per service (active, inactive, or expired) at a time.":"API keys grant access to specific AWS services. You can have a maximum of two API keys per service (active, inactive, or expired) at a time.","API keys provide programmatic access to specific AWS services. Store your key securely — it will not be shown again after generation.":"API keys provide programmatic access to specific AWS services. Store your key securely — it will not be shown again after generation.","Application assignments":"Application assignments","Application running on an AWS compute service":"Application running on an AWS compute service","Application running outside AWS":"Application running outside AWS",Applications:ai,Apply:si,"Apply customized password requirements.":"Apply customized password requirements.","Apply default password requirements.":"Apply default password requirements.","Archive rules":"Archive rules","Are you providing console access to a person?":"Are you providing console access to a person?","Are you providing console access to a person? Instead of creating an IAM user, we recommend that you add the person to your organization’s directory. To do so, you must be signed in as either the organization management account or the delegated administrator.":"Are you providing console access to a person? Instead of creating an IAM user, we recommend that you add the person to your organization’s directory. To do so, you must be signed in as either the organization management account or the delegated administrator.","Are you providing console access to a person? Instead of creating an IAM user, we recommend that your management account owner enable Identity Center for your organization so you can use an organizational directory to manage people's access to AWS accounts and applications.":"Are you providing console access to a person? Instead of creating an IAM user, we recommend that your management account owner enable Identity Center for your organization so you can use an organizational directory to manage people's access to AWS accounts and applications.","Are you sure you want to activate {{regionName}}?":"Are you sure you want to activate {{regionName}}?","Are you sure you want to close the window?":"Are you sure you want to close the window?","Are you sure you want to deactivate {{regionName}}?":"Are you sure you want to deactivate {{regionName}}?","Are you sure you want to delete the key pair with ID":"Are you sure you want to delete the key pair with ID","Are you sure you want to delete this key?":"Are you sure you want to delete this key?","Are you sure you want to leave the current page? The changes that you made won't be saved.":"Are you sure you want to leave the current page? The changes that you made won't be saved.","Are you sure you want to proceed with this trust policy?":"Are you sure you want to proceed with this trust policy?","Are you sure you want to update this trust policy?":"Are you sure you want to update this trust policy?",ARN:"ARN","as a backup. Ensure the new metadata file is correct. Incorrect metadata can prevent your identities from federating into this AWS account.":"as a backup. Ensure the new metadata file is correct. Incorrect metadata can prevent your identities from federating into this AWS account.","As a best practice, avoid using long-term credentials like access keys. Instead, use tools which provide short term credentials.":"As a best practice, avoid using long-term credentials like access keys. Instead, use tools which provide short term credentials.","As a best practice, delete roles that are no longer in use.":"As a best practice, delete roles that are no longer in use.","As a best practice, disable console access for inactive users.":"As a best practice, disable console access for inactive users.","As a best practice, enable MFA for users who have console access.":"As a best practice, enable MFA for users who have console access.","As a best practice, rotate your console password regularly.":"As a best practice, rotate your console password regularly.","As a best practice, use temporary security credentials (IAM roles) instead of creating long-term credentials like access keys, and don't create AWS account root user access keys.":"As a best practice, use temporary security credentials (IAM roles) instead of creating long-term credentials like access keys, and don't create AWS account root user access keys.","As a security best practice, we recommend having at least one MFA device registered.":"As a security best practice, we recommend having at least one MFA device registered.","As a security best practice, we recommend you assign MFA.":"As a security best practice, we recommend you assign MFA.",Assign:oi,"Assign an IAM role to compute resources like EC2 instances or Lambda functions to automatically supply temporary credentials to enable access.":"Assign an IAM role to compute resources like EC2 instances or Lambda functions to automatically supply temporary credentials to enable access.","Assign delegated administrator":"Assign delegated administrator","Assign delegated administrator for centralized root access":"Assign delegated administrator for centralized root access","Assign MFA":"Assign MFA","Assign MFA device":"Assign MFA device","Assign role":"Assign role","Assign role for {{idpName}}":"Assign role for {{idpName}}","Assign users and groups":"Assign users and groups","Assigned AWS account":"Assigned AWS account","Assigning delegated administrator.":"Assigning delegated administrator.","Associate an existing role by adding this IdP to the trusted entities of the role.":"Associate an existing role by adding this IdP to the trusted entities of the role.","At least one selection is required":"At least one selection is required",Attach:ni,"Attac