ng policy...":"Attaching policy...","Attributes your external identity provider dynamically asserts about a user or workload identifier during federation, carried in STS session tokens.":"Attributes your external identity provider dynamically asserts about a user or workload identifier during federation, carried in STS session tokens.",Audience:ii,"Audience {{audienceName}} deleted.":"Audience {{audienceName}} deleted.","Audience {{audienceName}} not added.":"Audience {{audienceName}} not added.","Audience {{audienceName}} not deleted.":"Audience {{audienceName}} not deleted.","Audience is required.":"Audience is required.","Audience selection":"Audience selection",Audiences:ri,"Audiences added. You must assign IAM roles to each to start using them.":"Audiences added. You must assign IAM roles to each to start using them.","Audiences not added.":"Audiences not added.","Authenticate your non AWS workloads and securely provide access to AWS services.":"Authenticate your non AWS workloads and securely provide access to AWS services.","Autogenerate or set a new custom password.":"Autogenerate or set a new custom password.","Autogenerated password":"Autogenerated password","Automatically reduce permissions":"Automatically reduce permissions","Available features":"Available features","Avoid using long-term credentials like access keys to improve your security. Consider the following use cases and alternatives.":"Avoid using long-term credentials like access keys to improve your security. Consider the following use cases and alternatives.","AWS account":"AWS account","AWS Account":"AWS Account","AWS account ID":"AWS account ID","AWS accounts":"AWS accounts","AWS accounts details":"AWS accounts details","AWS Certificate Manager Private Certificate Authority":"AWS Certificate Manager Private Certificate Authority","AWS CodeCommit credentials":"AWS CodeCommit credentials","AWS condition key":"AWS condition key","AWS condition key <2>(aws:TransactionContext/IdentityProvider/)</2>":"AWS condition key <2>(aws:TransactionContext/IdentityProvider/)</2>","AWS does not retain your private key. If you lose your private key, you must create a new key pair. For your protection, store your private key securely and do not share it.":"AWS does not retain your private key. If you lose your private key, you must create a new key pair. For your protection, store your private key securely and do not share it.","AWS Email address":"AWS Email address","AWS generates a thumbprint for the name of your certificate file. The thumbprint identifies your certificate in the Security Credentials page and is displayed as the access key ID in usage reports for your AWS account.":"AWS generates a thumbprint for the name of your certificate file. The thumbprint identifies your certificate in the Security Credentials page and is displayed as the access key ID in usage reports for your AWS account.","AWS GovCloud (US-East) Region endpoint":"AWS GovCloud (US-East) Region endpoint","AWS GovCloud (US-West) Region endpoint":"AWS GovCloud (US-West) Region endpoint","AWS IAM credentials":"AWS IAM credentials","AWS IAM Identity Center":"AWS IAM Identity Center","AWS managed":"AWS managed","AWS managed - job function":"AWS managed - job function","AWS maps the user or workload identifier and runtime claims you configure to context keys in the role session. AWS uses these context keys to authorize requests, record activity, calculate fees, and support cost allocation. The context keys do not constitute your content. AWS recommends that you do not include personally identifying, confidential, or sensitive information in the configured identifier or runtime claims.":"AWS maps the user or workload identifier and runtime claims you configure to context keys in the role session. AWS uses these context keys to authorize requests, record activity, calculate fees, and support cost allocation. The context keys do not constitute your content. AWS recommends that you do not include personally identifying, confidential, or sensitive information in the configured identifier or runtime claims.","AWS needs at least one private key if SAML assertion encryption is required. Update your encryption preference if you still want to remove this key.":"AWS needs at least one private key if SAML assertion encryption is required. Update your encryption preference if you still want to remove this key.","AWS Organizations":"AWS Organizations","AWS Organizations: AWS accounts":"AWS Organizations: AWS accounts","AWS Organizations: Organization Activity":"AWS Organizations: Organization Activity","AWS Organizations: Resource control policies (RCPs)":"AWS Organizations: Resource control policies (RCPs)","AWS Organizations: Service control policies (SCPs)":"AWS Organizations: Service control policies (SCPs)","AWS Organizations: Service Control Policies (SCPs)":"AWS Organizations: Service Control Policies (SCPs)","AWS recommends using regional STS endpoints to reduce latency. Session tokens from regional STS endpoints are valid in all AWS Regions. If you use regional STS endpoints, no action is required. Session tokens from the global STS endpoint ({{endpoint}}) are valid only in AWS Regions that are enabled by default. If you intend to enable a new Region for your account, you can use session tokens from regional STS endpoints or activate the global STS endpoint to issue session tokens that are valid in all AWS Regions.":"AWS recommends using regional STS endpoints to reduce latency. Session tokens from regional STS endpoints are valid in all AWS Regions. If you use regional STS endpoints, no action is required. Session tokens from the global STS endpoint ({{endpoint}}) are valid only in AWS Regions that are enabled by default. If you intend to enable a new Region for your account, you can use session tokens from regional STS endpoints or activate the global STS endpoint to issue session tokens that are valid in all AWS Regions.","AWS Region":"AWS Region","AWS Regions enabled by default":"AWS Regions enabled by default","AWS secures communication with Google’s OIDC identity provider (IdP) using our library of trusted CAs rather than using a certificate thumbprint to verify the server certificate of your IdP. Your legacy thumbprint(s) will remain in your configuration but will no longer be needed for validation.":"AWS secures communication with Google’s OIDC identity provider (IdP) using our library of trusted CAs rather than using a certificate thumbprint to verify the server certificate of your IdP. Your legacy thumbprint(s) will remain in your configuration but will no longer be needed for validation.","AWS secures communication with OIDC identity providers (IdP) that use an S3 bucket to host the JSON Web Key Set (JWKS) endpoint using our library of trusted CAs rather than using a certificate thumbprint to verify your IdP’s server certificate. Your legacy thumbprint(s) will remain in your configuration but will no longer be needed for validation.":"AWS secures communication with OIDC identity providers (IdP) that use an S3 bucket to host the JSON Web Key Set (JWKS) endpoint using our library of trusted CAs rather than using a certificate thumbprint to verify your IdP’s server certificate. Your legacy thumbprint(s) will remain in your configuration but will no longer be needed for validation.","AWS secures communication with OIDC identity providers (IdPs) using our library of trusted Certificate Authorities (CAs). If your IdP relies on a certificate that isn't signed by one of these trusted CAs, then we secure communication using the thumbprints you specify.":"AWS secures communication with OIDC identity providers (IdPs) using our library of trusted Certificate Authorities (CAs). If your IdP relies on a certificate that isn't signed by one of these trusted CAs, then we secure communication using the thumbprints you specify.","AWS secures communication with this OIDC identity provider (IdP) using our library of trusted CAs rather t