imum.":"IAM users switching roles in the console are granted a role session duration up to this value. API or CLI users can use the DurationSeconds parameter to set a session duration up to this maximum.","IAM users will still be able to use the default URL containing the AWS account ID.":"IAM users will still be able to use the default URL containing the AWS account ID.","IAM will use this key for decrypting your SAML assertions.":"IAM will use this key for decrypting your SAML assertions.","Icon for AWS Organizations service":"Icon for AWS Organizations service",ID:"ID",Identifier:rr,"Identifier of the account that can use this role":"Identifier of the account that can use this role","Identify the service and customize role-specific content.":"Identify the service and customize role-specific content.","Identities federating with this audience won’t be able to assume roles associated with this audience. Removing an audience does not delete the associated roles because they might have other trusted entities as well. We recommended that you":"Identities federating with this audience won’t be able to assume roles associated with this audience. Removing an audience does not delete the associated roles because they might have other trusted entities as well. We recommended that you","Identities from this provider won't be able to access this AWS account. Deleting a provider does not delete the associated roles because they might have other trusted entities as well. We recommended that you":"Identities from this provider won't be able to access this AWS account. Deleting a provider does not delete the associated roles because they might have other trusted entities as well. We recommended that you","Identity and Access Management (IAM)":"Identity and Access Management (IAM)","Identity attribute mappings":"Identity attribute mappings","Identity Center is enabled. We recommend managing workforce users' access to AWS accounts and cloud applications in Identity Center.":"Identity Center is enabled. We recommend managing workforce users' access to AWS accounts and cloud applications in Identity Center.","Identity propagation":"Identity propagation","Identity propagation settings for {{name}} have been updated.":"Identity propagation settings for {{name}} have been updated.","Identity provider":"Identity provider","Identity Provider":"Identity Provider","Identity provider deleted.":"Identity provider deleted.","Identity provider details":"Identity provider details","Identity provider is required.":"Identity provider is required.","Identity provider not deleted.":"Identity provider not deleted.","Identity provider was not added.":"Identity provider was not added.","Identity providers":"Identity providers","Identity Providers":"Identity Providers","Identity Providers and Federation":"Identity Providers and Federation","If checked, AWS will not accept non-encrypted SAML assertions.":"If checked, AWS will not accept non-encrypted SAML assertions.","If the public key associated with this private key is being used by your identity provider to encrypt SAML assertions, your workforce will be blocked from federating into this AWS account. You can add this private key again.":"If the public key associated with this private key is being used by your identity provider to encrypt SAML assertions, your workforce will be blocked from federating into this AWS account. You can add this private key again.","If you are creating programmatic access through access keys or service-specific credentials for AWS CodeCommit or Amazon Keyspaces, you can generate them after you create this IAM user.":"If you are creating programmatic access through access keys or service-specific credentials for AWS CodeCommit or Amazon Keyspaces, you can generate them after you create this IAM user.","If you choose Revoke active sessions, IAM attaches an inline policy named <b>AWSRevokeOlderSessions</b> to this role. This policy denies access to all currently active sessions for this role. You can continue to create new sessions based on this role. If you need to undo this action later, you can remove the inline policy.":"If you choose Revoke active sessions, IAM attaches an inline policy named <b>AWSRevokeOlderSessions</b> to this role. This policy denies access to all currently active sessions for this role. You can continue to create new sessions based on this role. If you need to undo this action later, you can remove the inline policy.","If you delete a certificate, any requests signed with it will fail. To make requests, you must create or upload a new certificate.":"If you delete a certificate, any requests signed with it will fail. To make requests, you must create or upload a new certificate.","If you lose or forget your secret access key, you cannot retrieve it. Instead, create a new access key and make the old key inactive.":"If you lose or forget your secret access key, you cannot retrieve it. Instead, create a new access key and make the old key inactive.","If you lose your private key, you must create or upload a new key pair. For your protection, store your key pair securely and do not share it.":"If you lose your private key, you must create or upload a new key pair. For your protection, store your key pair securely and do not share it.","If you want to give access to human users you can do so on your <link1>team page</link1>. IAM users should only be used for specific programmatic <link2>use cases</link2>.":"If you want to give access to human users you can do so on your <link1>team page</link1>. IAM users should only be used for specific programmatic <link2>use cases</link2>.","If you're providing console access to a person, it's a <link/> to manage their access in IAM Identity Center.":"If you're providing console access to a person, it's a <link/> to manage their access in IAM Identity Center.","If your use case requires an access key, create an IAM user with an access key and apply least privilege permissions for that user.":"If your use case requires an access key, create an IAM user with an access key and apply least privilege permissions for that user.","Important: The console does not support using an external ID with the Switch Role feature. If you select this option, entities in the trusted account must use the API, CLI, or a custom federation proxy to make cross-account iam:AssumeRole calls.":"Important: The console does not support using an external ID with the Switch Role feature. If you select this option, entities in the trusted account must use the API, CLI, or a custom federation proxy to make cross-account iam:AssumeRole calls.","Improved security":"Improved security","in {{timeGranularity}}":"in {{timeGranularity}}","In addition to console access, users with SignInLocalDevelopmentAccess permissions can use the same console credentials for programmatic access without the need for access keys.":"In addition to console access, users with SignInLocalDevelopmentAccess permissions can use the same console credentials for programmatic access without the need for access keys.","In addition to the management account, this member account will be authorized to have centralized root access for other member accounts.":"In addition to the management account, this member account will be authorized to have centralized root access for other member accounts.","In addition to the Organization management account, this member account will share administrator access for IAM.":"In addition to the Organization management account, this member account will share administrator access for IAM.","In progress":"In progress","in the field.":"in the field.",Inactive:cr,"Include a minimum of three of the following mix of character types:":"Include a minimum of three of the following mix of character types:","Include in the session context":"Include in the session context",info:lr,Info:dr,"Info about selected capabilities":"Info about selected capabilities","Info about trusted access":"Info about trust