ion tokens from the global endpoint ({{endpoint}}) valid in:":"Session tokens from the global endpoint ({{endpoint}}) valid in:","Session tokens from the STS endpoint in the Amazon Web Services China (Ningxia) Region support the use of the Sigv4a algorithm <a> Learn more </a> when signing Amazon Web Services requests. By default, session tokens from the STS endpoint in the Amazon Web Services China (Beijing) Region support only the Sigv4 algorithm for generating signatures. If you intend to use Sigv4a to cryptographically sign your Amazon Web Services requests, you can configure the STS endpoint in the Amazon Web Services China (Beijing) Region to vend session tokens that also support the Sigv4a algorithm.":"Session tokens from the STS endpoint in the Amazon Web Services China (Ningxia) Region support the use of the Sigv4a algorithm <a> Learn more </a> when signing Amazon Web Services requests. By default, session tokens from the STS endpoint in the Amazon Web Services China (Beijing) Region support only the Sigv4 algorithm for generating signatures. If you intend to use Sigv4a to cryptographically sign your Amazon Web Services requests, you can configure the STS endpoint in the Amazon Web Services China (Beijing) Region to vend session tokens that also support the Sigv4a algorithm.","Session tokens from the STS endpoint in the AWS GovCloud (US-East) Region support the use of the Sigv4a algorithm <a> Learn more </a> when signing Amazon Web Services requests. By default, session tokens from the STS endpoint in the AWS GovCloud (US-West) Region support only the Sigv4 algorithm for generating signatures. If you intend to use Sigv4a to cryptographically sign your Amazon Web Services requests, you can configure the STS endpoint in the AWS GovCloud (US-West) Region to vend session tokens that also support the Sigv4a algorithm.":"Session tokens from the STS endpoint in the AWS GovCloud (US-East) Region support the use of the Sigv4a algorithm <a> Learn more </a> when signin