r organization for managing root access on other member accounts. You can update the setting to delegate this privilege to another member account in your organization.","Use a permissions boundary to control the maximum permissions":"Use a permissions boundary to control the maximum permissions","Use a permissions boundary to control the maximum role permissions":"Use a permissions boundary to control the maximum role permissions","Use access keys to send programmatic calls to AWS from the AWS CLI, AWS Tools for PowerShell, AWS SDKs, or direct AWS API calls. You can have a maximum of two access keys (active or inactive) at a time.":"Use access keys to send programmatic calls to AWS from the AWS CLI, AWS Tools for PowerShell, AWS SDKs, or direct AWS API calls. You can have a maximum of two access keys (active or inactive) at a time.","Use an existing role":"Use an existing role","Use an identity provider (Idp) to manage your user identities outside of AWS, but grant the user identities permissions to use AWS resources in your account.":"Use an identity provider (Idp) to manage your user identities outside of AWS, but grant the user identities permissions to use AWS resources in your account.","Use an identity provider (IdP) to manage your user or workload identities outside of AWS, but grant those identities permissions to use AWS resources in your account.":"Use an identity provider (IdP) to manage your user or workload identities outside of AWS, but grant those identities permissions to use AWS resources in your account.","Use an Integrated Development Environment (IDE) which supports the AWS Toolkit enabling authentication through IAM Identity Center.":"Use an Integrated Development Environment (IDE) which supports the AWS Toolkit enabling authentication through IAM Identity Center.","Use an Integrated Development Environment (IDE) which supports the AWS Toolkit enabling authentication using your existing console credentials or IAM Identity Center.":"Use an Integrated Development Environment (IDE) which supports the AWS Toolkit enabling authentication using your existing console credentials or IAM Identity Center.","Use API keys for {{service}} to integrate into your library of choice and make API requests programmatically. You can have a maximum of two long-term API keys (active, inactive, or expired) at a time.":"Use API keys for {{service}} to integrate into your library of choice and make API requests programmatically. You can have a maximum of two long-term API keys (active, inactive, or expired) at a time.","Use AWS CLI V2 and the <code>aws login</code> command to use your existing console credentials in the CLI.":"Use AWS CLI V2 and the <code>aws login</code> command to use your existing console credentials in the CLI.","Use AWS CloudShell, a browser-based CLI, to run commands.":"Use AWS CloudShell, a browser-based CLI, to run commands.","Use case":"Use case","use cases":"use cases","Use existing policy":"Use existing policy","Use IAM Roles Anywhere to generate temporary security credentials for non AWS workloads accessing AWS services.":"Use IAM Roles Anywhere to generate temporary security credentials for non AWS workloads accessing AWS services.","Use MFA to increase the security of your AWS environment. Signing in with MFA requires an authentication code from an MFA device. Each user can have a maximum of 1 MFA device assigned.":"Use MFA to increase the security of your AWS environment. Signing in with MFA requires an authentication code from an MFA device. Each user can have a maximum of 1 MFA device assigned.","Use MFA to increase the security of your AWS environment. Signing in with MFA requires an authentication code from an MFA device. Each user can have a maximum of 8 MFA devices assigned.":"Use MFA to increase the security of your AWS environment. Signing in with MFA requires an authentication code from an MFA device. Each user can have a maximum of 8 MFA devices assigned.","Use only letters (A-Z, a-z), numbers (0-9), spaces, and these characters: _ . : / = + - @ #":"Use only letters (A-Z, a-z), numbers (0-9), spaces, and these characters: _ . : / = + - @ #","Use single spaces between words.":"Use single spaces between words.","Use SSH public keys to authenticate access to AWS CodeCommit repositories. You can have a maximum of five SSH public keys (active or inactive) at a time.":"Use SSH public keys to authenticate access to AWS CodeCommit repositories. You can have a maximum of five SSH public keys (active or inactive) at a time.","Use temporary credentials with ease and benefit from the enhanced security they provide.":"Use temporary credentials with ease and benefit from the enhanced security they provide.","Use the <a>AWS CLI V2</a> and enable authentication through a user in IAM Identity Center.":"Use the <a>AWS CLI V2</a> and enable authentication through a user in IAM Identity Center.","Use the JSON editor for more information about the character count.":"Use the JSON editor for more information about the character count.","Use this form to change your account email address.":"Use this form to change your account email address.","Use this form to change your password. Your new password must meet the requirements defined in the AWS account password policy.":"Use this form to change your password. Your new password must meet the requirements defined in the AWS account password policy.","Use this policy as a permissions boundary to control the maximum permissions that an entity can have. This is an advanced feature used to delegate permissions management to others.":"Use this policy as a permissions boundary to control the maximum permissions that an entity can have. This is an advanced feature used to delegate permissions management to others.","Use X.509 certificates to make secure SOAP-protocol requests to some AWS services. You can have a maximum of two X.509 certificates (active or inactive) at a time.":"Use X.509 certificates to make secure SOAP-protocol re