ed, but group-based access wasn't updated. To try again, choose Edit.",Username:Yc,users:$c,Users:Bc,"Users automatically get the <a>{{policyName}}</a> policy to allow them to change their own password.":"Users automatically get the <a>{{policyName}}</a> policy to allow them to change their own password.","Users deleted.":"Users deleted.","Users in this group":"Users in this group","Users must create a new password at next sign-in - Recommended":"Users must create a new password at next sign-in - Recommended","Users not deleted.":"Users not deleted.","Users table":"Users table","Using access keys attached to an IAM user instead of the root user improves security.":"Using access keys attached to an IAM user instead of the root user improves security.","Valid characters required.":"Valid characters required.","Valid in all AWS Regions":"Valid in all AWS Regions","Valid only in AWS Regions enabled by default":"Valid only in AWS Regions enabled by default","Valid until":"Valid until",Value:qc,"Value cannot be longer than {{AppIdMaxLength}} characters.":"Value cannot be longer than {{AppIdMaxLength}} characters.","Value*":"Value*",Values:Hc,Version:jc,"Version {{number}} of {{name}} deleted.":"Version {{number}} of {{name}} deleted.","Version {{numbers}} and {{last}} of {{name}} deleted.":"Version {{numbers}} and {{last}} of {{name}} deleted.","Version {{versionNumber}} of {{policyName}}":"Version {{versionNumber}} of {{policyName}}","Versions of this policy":"Versions of this policy","Videos, blog posts, and additional resources":"Videos, blog posts, and additional resources","View all":"View all","View all about What's New":"View all about What's New","View details":"View details","View details in IAM":"View details in IAM","View generated policy":"View generated policy","View group":"View group","View group {{groupName}}":"View group {{groupName}}","View permission details":"View permission details","View policy":"View policy","View policy JSON":"View policy JSON","View provider":"View provider","View role":"View role","View role {{roleName}}":"View role {{roleName}}","View roles":"View roles","View trust policy":"View trust policy","View user":"View user",Virtual:Qc,Warning:Xc,"Watch how it works":"Watch how it works","We are upgrading the infrastructure for the IAM console. The old experience will no longer be available after {{date}}. <a>Use the updated service console.</a>":"We are upgrading the infrastructure for the IAM console. The old experience will no longer be available after {{date}}. <a>Use the updated service console.</a>","We can't find a match.":"We can't find a match.","We could not summarize this policy.":"We could not summarize this policy.","We don't recommend that you create root user access keys. Because you can't specify the root user in a permissions policy, you can't limit its permissions, which is a best practice.":"We don't recommend that you create root user access keys. Because you can't specify the root user in a permissions policy, you can't limit its permissions, which is a best practice.","We recommend not to use the management account for managing root access of your member accounts, but delegate this privilege to a member account. You can update the setting to delegate this privilege to another member account in your organization.":"We recommend not to use the management account for managing root access of your member accounts, but delegate this privilege to a member account. You can update the setting to delegate this privilege to another member account in your organization.","We recommend removing your policy and role and then using the <b>custom role</b> creation flow. If this issue persists please contact support.":"We recommend removing your policy and role and then using the <b>custom role</b> creation flow. If this issue persists please contact support.","We recommend that you create IAM users only if you need to enable programmatic access through access keys, service-specific credentials for AWS CodeCommit or Amazon Keyspaces, or a backup credential for emergency account access.":"We recommend that you create IAM users only if you need to enable programmatic access through access keys, service-specific credentials for AWS CodeCommit or Amazon Keyspaces, or a backup credential for emergency account access.","We recommend that you use Identity Center to provide console access to a person. With Identity Center, you can centrally manage user access to their AWS accounts and cloud applications.":"We recommend that you use Identity Center to provide console access to a person. With Identity Center, you can centrally manage user access to their AWS accounts and cloud applications.","We recommend that you use Identity Center to provide console access to a person. With Identity Center, you can centrally manage user access to their AWS accounts and cloud applications. To do so, sign into the console by using the credentials of the management account in AWS Organizations, and then enable Identity Center. If you aren't the management account owner, contact the owner to perform this task.":"We recommend that you use Identity Center to provide console access to a person. With Identity Center, you can centrally manage user access to their AWS accounts and cloud applications. To do so, sign into the console by using the credentials of the management account in AWS Organizations, and then enable Identity Center. If you aren't the management account owner, contact the owner to perform this task.","We recommend that you use Identity Center to provide console access to a person. With Identity Center, you can centrally manage user access to their AWS accounts and cloud applications. To do so, you must be signed in to the Identity Center console using the credentials of the management account in AWS Organizations. If you aren't the management account owner, contact the owner to perform this task.":"We recommend that you use Identity Center to provide console access to a person. With Identity Center, you can centrally manage user access to their AWS accounts and cloud applications. To do so, you must be signed in to the Identity Center console using the credentials of the management account in AWS Organizations. If you aren't the management account owner, contact the owner to perform this task.","We recommend you":"We recommend you","We'll use your existing {{IdC}} account instance to look up your groups.":"We'll use your existing {{IdC}} account instance to look up your groups.","We'll use your existing {{IdC}} instance to look up your groups.":"We'll use your existing {{IdC}} instance to look up your groups.","We'll use your existing {{IdC}} organization instance to look up your groups.":"We'll use your existing {{IdC}} organization instance to look up your groups.","Web identity":"Web identity","Welcome to Amazon Web Services":"Welcome to Amazon Web Services","What's new":"What's new","When you enable root access management, you enable trusted access for IAM in AWS Organizations. <learnMore/>":"When you enable root access management, you enable trusted access for IAM in AWS Organizations. <learnMore/>","Widget behavior":"Widget behavior","Widget content":"Widget content","Widget preview":"Widget preview","Windows shell":"Windows shell","With group-based access, you can grant access to groups in AWS services, for example, {{lakeFormation}}, {{redshift}}, and {{s3AccessGrants}}.":"With group-based access, you can grant access to groups in AWS services, for example, {{lakeFormation}}, {{redshift}}, and {{s3AccessGrants}}.","Wrap lines":"Wrap lines",Write:Jc,"Write ({{count}} of {{totalCount}})_one":"Write ({{count}} of {{totalCount}})","Write ({{count}} of {{totalCount}})_other":"Write ({{count}} of {{totalCount}})","Write actions table":"Write actions table","X.509 certificate selection":"X.509 certificate selection","X.509 certificate successfully deleted.":"X.509 certificate successfully deleted.","X.509 certificate successfully uploaded.":"X.509 certificate successfully uploaded.","X.509 Signing certificates":"X.509 Signing certificates","X.509 Standard":"X.509 Standard",XML:"XML",Yes:"Yes","Yes, generate new policy":"Yes, generate new policy",Yesterday:Zc,"You are approaching your quota of available IAM resources.":"You are approaching your quota of available IAM resources.","You are revoking active console sessions for yourself. This action will immediately sign you out.":"You are revoking active console sessions for yourself. This action will immediately sign you out.","You are viewing the service access report for your organization’s master account. Service control policies do not apply to IAM principals in the master account. You will see a list of all services in the report.":"You are viewing the service access report for your organization’s master account. Service control policies do not apply to IAM principals in the master account. You will see a list of all services in the report.","You can add {{numLeft}} more audiences.":"You can add {{numLeft}} more audiences.","You can add {{remaining}} more tags.":"You can add {{remaining}} more tags.","You can add up to {{availableTags}} more tag.":"You can add up to {{availableTags}} more tag.","You can add up to {{availableTags}} more tags.":"You can add up to {{availableTags}} more tags.","You can add up to {{count}} more._one":"You can add up to {{count}} more.","You can add up to {{count}} more._other":"You can add up to {{count}} more.","You can add up to {{maxThumbprints}} thumbprints. This lets you maintain multiple thumbprints if the identity provider is rotating certificates.":"You can add up to {{maxThumbprints}} thumbprints. This lets you maintain multiple thumbprints if the identity provider is rotating certificates.","You can add up to {{numLeft}} more thumbprints.":"You can add up to {{numLeft}} more thumbprints.","You can add up to 1 more tag.":"You can add up to 1 more tag.","You can add, update, or remove thumbprints for this identity provider.":"You can add, update, or remove thumbprints for this identity provider.","You can attach up to {{number}} managed policies to this user group. All of the users in this group inherit the attached permissions.":"You can attach up to {{number}} managed policies to this user group. All of the users in this group inherit the attached permissions.","You can attach up to {{number}} managed policies.":"You can attach up to {{number}} managed policies.","You can attach up to {{number}} policies to this user group. All the users in this group will have permissions that are defined in the selected policies.":"You can attach up to {{number}} policies to this user group. All the users in this group will have permissions that are defined in the selected policies.","You can automatically reduce the permissions of roles that were created while Role Manager was enabled. Get started by looking at the findings column on the roles table.":"You can automatically reduce the permissions of roles that were created while Role Manager was enabled. Get started by looking at the findings column on the roles table.","You can delete and audit root credentials of member accounts. You can also allow password recovery for specific member accounts.":"You can delete and audit root credentials of member accounts. You can also allow password recovery for specific member accounts.","You can delete root credentials for member accounts and perform privileged actions from the management or delegated account. <a>Learn more about centralizing root access</a>":"You can delete root credentials for member accounts and perform privileged actions from the management or delegated account. <a>Learn more about centralizing root access</a>","You can delete root user credentials for member accounts and eliminate the need for managing long term root user credentials and associated multi-factor authentication (MFA) devices.":"You can delete root user credentials for member accounts and eliminate the need for managing long term root user credentials and associated multi-factor authentication (MFA) devices.","You can enable additional endpoints from which you can request temporary credentials. Activate only endpoints you intend to use.":"You can enable additional endpoints from which you can request temporary credentials. Activate only endpoints you intend to use.","You can generate a new policy based on the access activity for this {{resourceTypeText}}, then customize, create, and attach it to this role. AWS uses your CloudTrail events to identify the services and actions used and generate a policy.":"You can generate a new policy based on the access activity for this {{resourceTypeText}}, then customize, create, and attach it to this role. AWS uses your CloudTrail events to identify the services and actions used and generate a policy.","You can have a maximum of 2 private keys. Your identity provider will use the public key from the X.509 certificates for encrypting the SAML assertions. If you don’t specify any key, AWS will accept only unencrypted SAML assertions.":"You can have a maximum of 2 private keys. Your identity provider will use the public key from the X.509 certificates for encrypting the SAML assertions. If you don’t specify any key, AWS will accept only unencrypted SAML assertions.","You can have up to 5 versions of a customer managed policy.":"You can have up to 5 versions of a customer managed policy.",'You can increase the security of your role by requiring an optional external identifier, which prevents "confused deputy" attacks. This is recommended if you do not own or have administrative access to the account that can assume this role. The external ID can include any characters that you choose. To assume this role, users must be in the trusted account and provide this exact external ID.':'You can increase the security of your role by requiring an optional external identifier, which prevents "confused deputy" attacks. This is recommended if you do not own or have administrative access to the account that can assume this role. The external ID can include any characters that you choose. To assume this role, users must be in the trusted account and provide this exact external ID.',"You can now propagate identity context from your identity provider into IAM federated sessions. Use them for fine-grained access controls or auditing in CloudTrail.":"You can now propagate identity context from your identity provider into IAM federated sessions. Use them for fine-grained access controls or auditing in CloudTrail.","You can prove root credential non existence for your audit and compliance needs, proving your root user is secured across your member accounts.":"You can prove root credential non existence for your audit and compliance needs, proving your root user is secured across your member accounts.","You can select one of the existing permissions policies to define the boundary.":"You can select one of the existing permissions policies to define the boundary.","You can take certain root actions in member accounts like deleting misconfigured policies in Amazon SQS or Amazon S3.":"You can take certain root actions in member accounts like deleting misconfigured policies in Amazon SQS or Amazon S3.","You can take certain root actions in member accounts like deleting misconfigured policies in Amazon SQS, or Amazon S3.":"You can take certain root actions in member accounts like deleting misconfigured policies in Amazon SQS, or Amazon S3.","You can use these credentials when connecting from your local computer, or from tools that require a static user name and password.":"You can use these credentials when connecting from your local computer, or from tools that require a static user name and password.","You can view and download the user’s password and email instructions for signing in to the AWS Management Console.":"You can view and download the user’s password and email instructions for signing in to the AWS 